{"blocks":[["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-817","Convert #tag links to [[wikilink]] form on commit",["Ideas"]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-877","I'd like a pre-commit converter, built like the text:fix-invisible mise task, that rewrites Logseq #tag and #[[Page]] links into [[...]] form — one obvious way to link (Py/Zen of Python), and the shape Looksyk can import, since it reads [[...]] but not #tag.",["Ideas","Convert #tag links to [[wikilink]] form on commit"]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-1162","Not as safe a rewrite as invisible whitespace, so it stays deferred. A # also begins headings, hex colors, shell comments, and URL fragments, so the converter has to skip fenced and inline code, ignore # before a space or another #, and treat # as a link only at a word boundary. Scope it to .md files under pages/ and journals/, where well over a thousand inline # links live today.",["Ideas","Convert #tag links to [[wikilink]] form on commit"]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-1576","fail2ban",[]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-1592","Person/James Clear",[]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-1618","Person/James Clear/Book/18/Atomic Habits",[]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-1666","Person/James Clear/Book/18/Atomic Habits/Quote/Good Easy, Bad Difficult",[]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-1745","My/Principle/Make the Right Thing Easy and the Wrong Thing Hard",[]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-1871","Py/Zen of Python",[]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-1895","My/Principle/Simplify/Not every distinction is worth recording",[]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-1965","Terminal/Multiplexer/Idea",[]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-1998","Logseq/Entity/Dotfiles/Dep/Idea",[]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-2037","Updated",[]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-2053","dependency intake vision",["Updated"]],["p-fd669bdec159f136.html","source-block-2081"